-- title:
--   Single remaining occupancy characterizes transversals
-- statement:
--   Let $n\in\mathbb N$, $E=\{0,\ldots,n-1\}$, and $\widehat E=E\times\{0,1\}$. A partial assignment $\sigma:E\to\{*,0,1\}$ has assigned set $A_\sigma=\{i:\sigma_i\ne *\}$ and selected-label set $C_\sigma=\{(i,\sigma_i):i\in A_\sigma\}$. A paired state respects $\sigma$ when it includes the selected label and excludes its mate at every assigned pair. For $U\subseteq E$, write $O_{\sigma,U}=\sum_{i\notin A_\sigma\cup U}\mathbf e_i$, where $\mathbf e_i$ is the unit exponent at $i$. Write $[x^d]g$ for the coefficient of exponent vector $d$ in a polynomial $g$. Let $S\subseteq\widehat E$ respect $\sigma$ and put $$v_\sigma(S)_i=\bigl|\{b\in\{0,1\}:(i,b)\in S\setminus C_\sigma\}\bigr|.$$ Then $$v_\sigma(S)=O_{\sigma,\varnothing}\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad S\text{ contains exactly one label from every pair}. $$ Equivalently, for every $i$, membership of $(i,0)$ is equivalent to nonmembership of $(i,1)$. This identifies the transversal coefficient pattern after conditioning.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/ConditionalOccupancyCoefficients.lean#L92-L118

